<title>UK: UK Q4 C/A surplus 873 mln stg.</title>
<headline>UK Q4 C/A surplus 873 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics issued the following seasonally adjusted, fourth quarter current account data. (deficit denoted by minus sign)</p>
<p>    Figures in million stg	  Q4	  Q3		Q4 1995</p>
<p>    Current account	     873	 -293  (-71)    -1,176</p>
<p>    Trade in goods	    -2,581    -2,913  (-2,928) -3,192</p>
<p>    Trade in services	  1,935*    1,697  (1,768)   1,611</p>
<p>    Investment income	  2,587     1,918  (1,891)   2,456</p>
<p>    Transfers		   -1,068	-995  (-802)   -2,051</p>
<p>    UK investment overseas  -8,156    -4,690  (-4,088) -7,852</p>
<p>    Overseas invtmnt in UK   6,230     5,199  (5,038)   7,015</p>
<p>The ONS said the UK posted a current account deficit of 14 million stg in 1996 as a whole, following a deficit of 3,743 million in 1995.</p>
<p>Market forecast a Q4 current account deficit of 400 million stg, and a trade in goods deficit of 2.6 billion stg.</p>
<p>* The trade in services surplus was the highest quarterly surplus on record, the ONS said.</p>
</text>
